6,About: Xamtanga language,https://dbpedia.org/page/Xamtanga_language,"Xamtanga (also Agawinya, Khamtanga, Simt'anga, Xamir, Xamta) is a Central Cushitic language spoken in Ethiopia by the Xamir people.",Xamtanga,Afro-Asiatic
7,"From jazz to hip hop, Afro-South Asian music collaborations reflect imagined, more liberatory worlds",https://scroll.in/article/987321/from-jazz-to-hip-hop-afro-south-asian-music-collaborations-reflect-imagined-more-liberatory-worlds,"February 21, 2021 - Sounds from the Other Side: Afro-South Asian Collaborations in Black Popular Music opens with a succinct yet compelling dedication: “To the Power of Black music.” As the introduction explains, you envisioned the book as an investigation of Black and South Asian (American) musical collaborations that are revealing of Blackness, Black politics, and Black cultural expression.",Xamtanga,Afro-Asiatic
